---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Doc from '../components/legal/Doc.astro';
const updated = '30 October 2026';
// Shows a draft note and keeps the page out of search until the placeholders are filled (design/legal/README.md).
const draft = true;
---

<Base title="Creator agreement · Comarket" description="The agreement for creators on Comarket: how sales count, when you get paid, taxes, disclosure, the rules, your content and your right to say no." stage="none" noindex={draft}>
  <Doc
    title="Creator agreement"
    lede="Comarket is free for creators, and you get paid on every sale you send. This is the agreement behind that."
    updated={updated}
    draft={draft}
    current="/creator-terms"
  >
    <div class="short">
      <b>The short version</b>
      <ul>
        <li>You never pay Comarket. Brands pay us.</li>
        <li>You earn the rate you accepted on each completed sale from a buyer new to the brand, and on their renewals for 12 months.</li>
        <li>We pay you monthly through Stripe, after the brand's refund window closes.</li>
        <li>Say clearly in every post that you earn from the link. Never buy through your own link.</li>
        <li>Turn down any brand, or stop promoting one, whenever you like.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>1. This agreement</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">1.1</span>This agreement is between [[LEGAL ENTITY NAME]] ("Comarket", "we") and you, the creator who accepts it
      when opening an account. The general terms in <a href="/terms#general-terms">section 7 of the Terms of use</a> are part of
      it. Words like Offer, Storefront, First Payment, Renewal, Commission Period, Net Amount and Refund Window mean what
      section 2 of the <a href="/brand-terms">Brand Agreement</a> says.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">1.2</span>You must be 18 or older and able to receive payouts through Stripe. You work as an independent
      contractor, not our employee, and you're free to work with any other brand or platform.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Free, with your own page</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">2.1</span>Comarket is free for creators. We charge you no fees and cover Stripe's fees for sending your
      payouts.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">2.2</span>You get a page at comarket.si/your-handle and a Storefront for each Offer you accept and the brand
      approves. We may withdraw a handle that impersonates someone or uses a name you have no right to, and will offer you
      another. A closed account's handle stays unused for 90 days.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Your right to say no</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.1</span>Brands send Offers with the product, what buyers get, your rate and the Refund Window. Accept or
      decline any Offer, without a reason. Declining never counts against you.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.2</span>You may stop promoting an Offer at any time; we take its Storefront down within 2 business days. A
      brand may also withdraw its approval. Checkouts started before a Storefront comes down still count.
    </p>

    <h2>4. What counts as a sale</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">4.1</span>You earn on a completed payment by a buyer who started checkout from your Storefront, paid within 30
      days of their last visit to it, is new to the brand, and didn't get a full refund within the Refund Window. Section 4 of
      the <a href="/brand-terms">Brand Agreement</a> has the full test.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">4.2</span>A buyer isn't new if their email, phone number or card fingerprint matches one of the brand's
      existing Stripe customers. Your dashboard shows every sale and, when one doesn't count, why, but never who the buyer was.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Getting paid</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.1</span>For each sale that counts, you earn your rate on the First Payment and on each Renewal for 12 months,
      unless the Offer pays on the First Payment only.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.2</span>Earnings on a payment are confirmed when its Refund Window closes. A partial refund reduces them in
      proportion.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.3</span>By the 15th of each month, we pay your confirmed earnings that the brand has paid us, in US dollars,
      to your bank through a Stripe connected account, if they total at least $25. Smaller amounts carry over; when you close
      your account, we pay any balance. You need to accept Stripe's Connected Account Agreement and complete its identity
      checks.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.4</span>The brand owes you your earnings. You appoint us as your limited agent to collect them; once the brand
      pays us, we owe them to you. If a brand pays late, we pay you at the next payout after it pays. We chase late brands and
      pass on everything we recover.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.5</span>If a buyer wins a chargeback within 120 days of a payment, or a sale turns out to break section 8, we
      deduct those earnings from future payouts. We ask you to repay directly only if the sale broke section 8.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.6</span>You may question any sale or payout within 60 days by writing to [[CONTACT EMAIL]]. A person reviews it
      and replies within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Taxes</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">6.1</span>You're responsible for taxes on your earnings. US creators provide a Form W-9 through Stripe, and we or
      Stripe issue a Form 1099 where the law requires. Non-US creators provide the tax form Stripe requests. We may withhold tax
      where the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Disclosing that you earn</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.1</span>Every time you promote an Offer (a post, story, video, newsletter, podcast or message), say clearly
      that you earn from it, as the FTC's Endorsement Guides (16 CFR Part 255) require:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>at the start, in plain words like "Ad", "Paid link" or "I earn a commission if you buy", not buried in hashtags or behind "more";</li>
      <li>in video and audio, out loud as well as on screen;</li>
      <li>using the platform's paid-partnership label too, where it has one.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.2</span>Only say what you really think, don't say you use a product unless you do, and make only the claims the
      Offer allows. Follow your platform's rules, and the rules of your audience's country. Every Storefront also shows that
      you earn a commission; don't hide it.
    </p>

    <h2>8. The rules</h2>
    <p><span class="n">8.1</span>You must not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>buy through your own link,</b> or have someone in your household or acting for you do so;</li>
      <li><b>pay or reward buyers</b> to buy, such as sharing your commission or cashback, unless the Offer allows it;</li>
      <li><b>stuff cookies or force clicks</b> with hidden frames, pop-unders, redirects, extensions or adware;</li>
      <li><b>post codes or links on coupon or deal sites,</b> unless the Offer allows it;</li>
      <li><b>spam:</b> unsolicited emails, texts or messages, or links where a community forbids them;</li>
      <li><b>bid on a brand's name</b> in search or social ads, or use it in a domain or account name, without the brand's written permission;</li>
      <li><b>pose as the brand</b> or as an ordinary customer, or post fake reviews;</li>
      <li><b>make misleading claims,</b> including about health, money or results the Offer doesn't allow;</li>
      <li><b>use bots,</b> fake followers or bought engagement, or misstate your audience;</li>
      <li><b>target children,</b> or promote in content made for them;</li>
      <li><b>get around the new-customer check</b> with made-up identities or extra accounts; or</li>
      <li><b>post content that's illegal,</b> sexually explicit, hateful or harassing, or that infringes someone else's rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <span class="n">8.2</span>Sales that come from breaking these rules don't count, and we may withhold or reverse the earnings on
      them. For a serious or repeated breach we may also end your account. We'll tell you what we did and why, and you can ask
      a person to review it at [[CONTACT EMAIL]].
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your content</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">9.1</span>You own your content, name and likeness. You let us host, display and resize your name, handle, photo,
      bio, public profile stats and the content you add, to run your page and Storefronts and to show your profile and results
      to brands you're matched with, while your account is open.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">9.2</span>We feature you in Comarket's own marketing only with your permission. A brand may use your content
      outside its Storefronts only if you agree.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">9.3</span>You confirm you have the rights to what you add and that anyone shown in it agreed. You may use a
      brand's names, logos and materials only to promote its Offer while you're approved.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Buyers' data</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">10.1</span>We never give you buyers' identities. If a buyer contacts you directly, handle their information
      lawfully. Our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> covers your own data.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Ending</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">11.1</span>You may close your account at any time; we take your page and Storefronts down within 2 business days.
      We may end this agreement with 30 days' notice, or at once for a serious breach or fraud.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">11.2</span>Unless it ends for your fraud or serious breach, you keep earning on sales made before the end,
      including their Renewals for the rest of each 12 months, and we keep paying you monthly. You don't have to delete old
      posts.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">12.1</span>You will compensate us for third-party claims arising from your content, missing disclosures,
      breaking section 8, or your taxes.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">12.2</span>Neither side is liable for lost profits or indirect, incidental or consequential damages. Our total
      liability to you is limited to what we paid you in the 12 months before the claim. This doesn't limit our duty to pay you
      earnings we've collected for you, or liability for fraud or willful misconduct.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">12.3</span>Sections 5, 6, 8.2, 9.3, 11.2 and 12 survive the end of this agreement.
    </p>
  </Doc>
  <Footer />
</Base>
